id: sheath-holster
name: Sheath/Holster
kind: gear
itemType: accessory
craftDC: Qualified
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Holds a Weapon. Drawn the first time in an Encounter, the next Strike with it that Round is
  2(T) higher; sheathed at an Encounter's end, it regains 1/4 of its Life Points.
text: >
  Sheath/Holster: You can store a Weapon in this Accessory for ease of travel.
  –Craft DC: Qualified
  –Effects: When you sheathe a Weapon, you may store it within this Accessory. When you
  unsheathe your Weapon from this Accessory for the first time in a Combat Encounter, increase
  your next Strike Roll made for an Armed Attack with that Weapon during this Combat Round by
  2(T).

  At the end of each Combat Encounter, if you sheathe your Weapon into this Accessory, that
  Weapon regains 1/4 of its Life Points. This effect does not apply if the Weapon is destroyed.

  If this Item is stolen or lost while a Weapon is sheathed inside of it, the Weapon remains in
  the Item and is stolen/lost as well.

---

# --- What is built -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Accessory itself: given, worn and taken off like any other.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Everything it does is about a Weapon, and there are no Weapons in this system yet - they
# arrive with Equipment. When they do:
#
# Sheathe: a Weapon of the character's stored in it, one at a time - shown on its row the way a
# Capsule shows what it holds, and moving with it: "the Weapon remains in the Item and is
# stolen/lost as well."
#
# Unsheathe: the first time in a Combat Encounter, the next Strike Roll of an Armed Attack with
# that Weapon this Combat Round is 2(T) higher - a mark with the Round's clock, spent by that
# Strike. Once an Encounter, kept with the other once-per-Encounter uses.
#
# The Encounter's end: a Weapon sheathed then, and not destroyed, regains 1/4 of its Life
# Points.
